  "description": "Instructional tg/ctg reduction table: four columns, blank numbering header and three individually ruled data rows. Exact tg/ctg spelling, signs and stacked fractions are retained. Coordinates, spacing and line weights are unmeasured modern typesetting regularization. The original angle glyph is a/alpha-shaped and alphabetically unresolved in the pixel inventory; Greek alpha follows the approved official context, not an asserted pixel code-point identification. No additional values, conditions, answers or captions.",
